\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{What the two forms distinguish}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The same sign connections give the positive marginal
of \ref{fdip-00XZ} and the negative matter insertion of
\ref{fdip-00XY}. The latter is already even, locally gauge
invariant and strictly supported in the positive half.
Neither a restriction excluding odd observables nor a
choice to leave boundary-edge fields outside that half
removes it.}

\p{These conclusions concern the declared cellular
anti-reflection and full cochain operator. They give no
positivity statement for arbitrary reflection-paired gauge
averages and no obstruction to a different, explicitly
constructed fermionic reflection or transfer operator.}
